<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila shares end shade up on bargain-hunting.</title>
<headline>Manila shares end shade up on bargain-hunting.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>------------------------- Nov 4 -----------------------------</p>
<p>* Metrobank and Petron lift main index</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Manila shares ended slightly up on Monday after a slow opening, shored up by bargain hunting in selected blue chips, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market was up because of some bargain hunting and steady positioning,&quot; said Jonas Ferrer, research director at Pryce Securities Inc.</p>
<p>The main index closed up 12.14 points, or 0.41 percent, at 2,976.14 points.</p>
